cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite VIGIL Observatory and CAM Initiative using this dataset metadata. Public availability does not grant permission for substantive reuse. See LICENSE.md for the proprietary terms."
title: "VIGIL Observatory: AI Governance Incident Corpus and Alignment Taxonomy"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Rourke"
    given-names: "Michelle"
    affiliation: "CAM Initiative"
abstract: >
  VIGIL Observatory is CAM Initiative's evidence-linked and versioned research
  corpus of AI-governance Incidents, with occurrence-level diagnosis, the
  Alignment Taxonomy, harm assessment, external-governance interpretations,
  provenance and validation materials. Version 1.0.0 comprises 200
  canonical Incident records and published Alignment Taxonomy v0.8.1.
  Individual Incidents may retain earlier taxonomy editions or unresolved
  evidence states. The corpus is principally AI-assisted and human-governed;
  its contents are not independently human-certified or legal determinations.
keywords:
  - "AI governance"
  - "AI incidents"
  - "alignment taxonomy"
  - "incident analysis"
  - "evidence provenance"
  - "harm assessment"
  - "AI assurance"
  - "VIGIL Observatory"
publisher: "CAM Initiative"
